1	// THE LABEL VOCABULARY'S DECODE (tasks-dispatch DESIGN §4; the migration of #1119).
2	// Labels are stored data: an open item wears whatever the engine that filed it
3	// wrote, and a member converges on its own schedule. So every reader decodes, and
4	// what these tests pin is that ONE pass maps every spelling ever written straight
5	// to today's — plus the two places that would silently strand a member if they
6	// disagreed: the ensure-list (a label that does not exist 422s the write that
7	// applies it) and the executor workflow's literal event trigger.
